.Dd November 14, 2026
.Dt RAVEN-SVC 1
.Os RavenBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm raven-svc
.Nd list, inspect and control RavenBSD services
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Cm list
.Nm
.Cm status Ar name
.Nm
.Cm start Ar name
.Nm
.Cm stop Ar name
.Nm
.Cm restart Ar name
.Nm
.Cm enable Ar name
.Nm
.Cm disable Ar name
.Nm
.Cm logs Ar name
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is the modern front end to the
.Xr init 8
service control protocol.
It never kills a process directly, never reads a PID file and never scrapes
.Pa /proc .
.Pp
The commands are:
.Bl -tag -width "restart"
.It Cm list
List every service.
.It Cm status Ar name
Print one service.
.It Cm start Ar name
Start a stopped service.
.It Cm stop Ar name
Stop the service through the control protocol and wait for terminal state.
.It Cm restart Ar name
Stop the service and start a fresh instance.
.It Cm enable Ar name
Add the service to the sorted
.Pa /etc/raven/services.enable
file; the shipped manifest is not edited.
.It Cm disable Ar name
Remove the service from the enable file.
.It Cm logs Ar name
Alias for the log command; it is unavailable until the log crate is wired.
.El
.Pp
Every mutating command reports
.Va changed :
true or false in JSON and is idempotent.
The legacy
.Xr svcctl 1
front end keeps its existing text output and uses the same control protocol.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
An unavailable backend or a control failure exits 1; a usage error exits 2.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr raven 1 ,
.Xr svcctl 1 ,
.Xr init 8
.Sh STANDARDS
RavenBSD modern userland contract, revision 1.
